#{[17592186542016 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186541592 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542016 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186541617 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542016 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186541634 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542016 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186541739 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542016 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186541772 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542016 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542016 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542016 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186541617 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542016 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "5fa9844e-bf08-5151-a0ef-3ca82c6b8c21" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542017 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186541473 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542017 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186541585 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542017 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186541694 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542017 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186541770 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542017 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186541957 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542017 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542017 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542017 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186541585 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542017 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "60e99a5a-7fef-5572-9023-63b84b45c7f5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542082 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186541487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542082 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186541650 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542082 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186541858 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542082 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186541881 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542082 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186541946 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542082 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542082 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542082 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186541487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542082 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "e60fe765-3ba7-5b2e-a3cc-67f6b659f5d1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542136 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186542017 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542136 #edb/ref 1069 "q-119166" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542136 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542136 #edb/ref 1071 "The volume of a cylinder decreases at a rate that's proportional to the square of its radius. Write down a differential equation describing the rate of change of the radius, $r(t),$ in this process. Assume that the height of the cylinder does not change and that $K>0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542136 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3da31f55-8d6c-5a19-aa68-60451055a7de" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542136 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The **volume** of a cylinder **decreases** at a rate that's **proportional** to the **square of its radius**.*\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *volume $V$ of a cylinder* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}$ *decreases* at a rate that's *proportional to the square of its radius.* Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=-k{r}^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0.$\n\nWe wish to use this information to find an expression for $\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}.$\n\nThe volume $V$ of a cylinder is given by\n\n$$\nV=\\pi {r}^{2}h.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating this equation with respect to $t,$ and the fact that the height of the cylinder does not change, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\pi {r}^{2}h) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =2\\pi hr\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =-k{r}^{2} \\\\ 2\\pi hr\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =-k{r}^{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =-\\frac{k{r}^{2}}{2\\pi hr} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =-\\frac{kr}{2\\pi h}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now introduce a new constant:\n\n$$\nK=\\frac{k}{2\\pi h}>0\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, our equation becomes\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}=-Kr.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542145 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186542016 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542145 #edb/ref 1069 "q-143140" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542145 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542145 #edb/ref 1071 "At each point $P$ on a particular curve, the derivative ${y}^{′}(x)$ is **inversely** proportional to the shortest distance from $P$ to the $y$-axis. The derivative at the point $(2,8)$ equals $5.$ What differential equation describes this curve?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542145 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "500cc9b6-df77-5d16-8dd2-a74988fb81dd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542145 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*At each point $P$ on a particular curve, the **derivative** ${y}^{′}(x)$ is **inversely proportional** to the **shortest distance from $P$ to the $y$-axis**.*\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The *shortest distance from $P$ to the $y$-axis* is given by $|x|.$\n\n- Since the *derivative* is *inversely proportional* to the shortest distance from $P$ to the $y$-axis, we have \n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(x)=k\\cdot \\frac{1}{|x|}\n$$\n\nwhere $k$ is a constant.\n\nSo, our differential equation is\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(x)=\\frac{k}{|x|}.\n$$\n\nIn addition, we're told that ${y}^{′}(x)=5$ when at the point $(2,8).$ We can use this to determine the value of the coefficient $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5=\\frac{k}{|2|}\\,⟹\\,k=10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the differential equation describing the curve is\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}(x)=\\frac{10}{|x|}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542180 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186541987 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542180 #edb/ref 1069 "q-119170" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542180 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542180 #edb/ref 1071 "The volume of a cylinder decreases at a rate proportional to its volume. Write down a differential equation describing the rate of change of the height, $h(t),$ in this process. \nAssume that the radius of the cylinder does not change and that $k>0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542180 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a29a3c61-aa9f-590b-908a-6227844310f9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542180 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The **volume** of a cylinder **decreases** at a rate **proportional** to its **volume**. *\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *volume $V$ of a cylinder* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}$ *decreases* at a rate *proportional to the volume.* Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t}=-kV,\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0.$\n\nWe wish to use this information to find an expression for $\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t}.$\n\nThe volume $V$ of a cylinder is given by\n\n$$\nV=\\pi {r}^{2}h.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating this equation with respect to $t,$ and using the fact that the radius of the cylinder does not change, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\pi {r}^{2}h) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =\\pi {r}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}V}{\\text{d}t} & =-kV \\\\ \\pi {r}^{2}\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t} & =-k(\\pi {r}^{2}h) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t} & =-\\frac{k\\pi {r}^{2}h}{\\pi {r}^{2}} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}t} & =-kh.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542182 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186542082 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542182 #edb/ref 1069 "q-143132" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542182 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542182 #edb/ref 1071 "The area of a circle decreases at a rate that's proportional to the cube of its radius. Write down a differential equation describing the rate of change of the radius, $r(t),$ in this process. Assume that $K>0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542182 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a8d62c5b-3e1c-59af-b194-160b1241f14c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542182 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's highlight the important words in the given statement:\n\n*The **area** of a circle **decreases** at a **rate** that's **proportional** to the cube of its **radius**. *\n\nWe note the following:\n\n- The question describes the *rate* at which the *area $A$ of a circle* varies. Therefore, this is a statement about the quantity \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}.\n$$\n\n- We're told that $\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}$ *decreases* at a rate that's *proportional* to the cube of its *radius.* In other words,\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=-k{r}^{3}\n$$\n\nwhere $k>0.$\n\nWe wish to use this information to find an expression for $\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}.$\n\nThe area of a circle is given by \n\n$$\nA=\\pi {r}^{2}.\n$$\n\n \n\nDifferentiating this equation with respect to $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\pi {r}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =2\\pi r\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t} & =-k{r}^{3} \\\\ 2\\pi r\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =-k{r}^{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =-\\frac{k{r}^{3}}{2\\pi r} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t} & =-\\frac{k{r}^{2}}{2\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now introduce a new constant:\n\n$$\nK=\\frac{k}{2\\pi }>0\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, our equation becomes\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}r}{\\text{d}t}=-K{r}^{2}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542238 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186542255 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542238 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "1a243f40-c3c6-58d7-bac3-52d3bb082cf4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542238 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186542182 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542243 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2b8f298c-89ca-5efd-8419-026734b35b16" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542243 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186542145 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542255 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186542243 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542255 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "52ea8b3b-19b7-5968-bcaa-348c34bcb384" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542255 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186373862 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542256 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186542238 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542256 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "53b991cc-3a22-5116-adab-cd17f3c705cb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542256 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186542180 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542271 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186542256 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542271 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "88e7fdbd-88d3-5a0c-b233-89990b64230f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542271 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186542136 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
